WEBVTT

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:03.842
Tessa wants to help new students find
their way around

00:00:03.842 --> 00:00:07.503
school. She compares making an
illustrated guide to the whole

00:00:07.503 --> 00:00:11.165
school with testing one page about a
single hard to

00:00:11.165 --> 00:00:11.897
find room.

00:00:12.380 --> 00:00:17.850
Relevance asks why the project matters.
Both ideas could help

00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:21.678
new students, and Tessa enjoys making
illustrations.

00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:25.827
Feasibility asks what Tessa could begin
with the time and

00:00:25.827 --> 00:00:29.674
resources she has. One page can start
with a sketch

00:00:29.674 --> 00:00:31.983
and feedback from a trusted adult.

00:00:32.380 --> 00:00:36.476
Scope asks how focused the idea is. A
guide to

00:00:36.476 --> 00:00:40.571
the entire school may be too big for the
first

00:00:40.571 --> 00:00:43.848
attempt. One room gives Tessa a clear
boundary.

00:00:44.180 --> 00:00:48.228
Tessa chooses the smaller guide. She
gives up wide coverage

00:00:48.228 --> 00:00:52.275
for now and gains a first draft she can
learn

00:00:52.275 --> 00:00:56.323
from. Use these lenses when you compare
your own directions.

